{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/129915-science-and-were-creatures","id":129915,"title":"Science and Were-creatures?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-10T08:50:42-07:00","id":129915,"title":"Science and Were-creatures?","content":"Hello all, I'm currently running a game of Hunter:tV in which a PC(a mortician) is attempting to determine how a were-elk(not a Forsaken, I know, but similar.) is capable of regeneration. Being not a particularly biology-oriented person, I'm at a bit of a loss to even attempt explaining their regeneration via science. Has anyone handled this themselves, or know of a book where WW covered it themselves? Any help is appreciated!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2975-fullplatehero","name":"FullPlateHero","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T09:17:29-07:00","id":129921,"title":"","content":"Sience is not going to help much, unless he is capable of using it to percieve and analize Essence. Because that's how regeneration works, the shifter takes small amounts of Essence from the ambience and regrows tissue by turning it into flesh and bone. Or alternatively it spends its own inner reserves of the stuff in a more direct and quick way.<br /> <br /> From the point of view of science, the best he is gonna get is that they have an imposibly fast metabolism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T09:29:50-07:00","id":129924,"title":"","content":"That being said, if you're playing Hunter, the explanation you can give is whatever you want it to be. <br /> <br /> I'd be inclined to agree with Thorbes, though: it should like a normal healing process jacked up to an absurd degree. You can note that there's no way of explaining where the energy that's power the cell division is coming from (Essence) as well as saying that it extends to ALL parts of the body -- even those which normally can't be rebuilt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1097-underwoodfive","name":"underwoodfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1097_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T09:40:24-07:00","id":129930,"title":"","content":"While Thorbes sums up the basics, Blood of the Wolf goes in-depth on the subject of werewolf regeneration. What a scientist will see is a vastly faster healing process than the human norm - one that is capable of completely repairing nerve damage, lost organs and limbs, and that is, to a certain extent, under the were-creature's conscious control (specifically when it comes to replacing lost organs and limbs).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T10:04:27-07:00","id":129947,"title":"","content":"Since you're playing Hunter, you're definitely not bound by the metaphysics of Forsaken and are free to make it an entirely biological process. You could, for example, say that shapeshifter a have a unique cellular structure that allows their cells to re-shape themselves according to what ever material is needed. Kind of like how embryonic stem cells can develop into different kinds of cells depending on the surrounding tissue, only amped up to 11. That would combine the shape-changing ability and the fast healing into a single process. (Also, I know next to nothing about how cells work, I just pulled all of that out of my ass. But it's not too difficult to make bogus science sound good to people who don't know the subject. And it's a fictional game, the people who know better can forgive inaccuracies for the sake of the fiction.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T10:16:40-07:00","id":129959,"title":"","content":"There's also the matter of what, exactly, said scientist has the capability to observe given his facilities and subject's opinion on being a test subject.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T21:50:19-07:00","id":131540,"title":"","content":"This is fantastic, guys. My Player actually has a Bachelor's in Biology, so BS'ing him isn't advisable. This will definitely help me give him something, though. <br /> <br /> Also, I'm aware Hunter doesn't have to use the supernatural templates for antagonists, but for the big-name monsters, anything less feels cheap to me. (I use the Dread Powers, etc. and spitball all the time for homebrew critters though.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2975-fullplatehero","name":"FullPlateHero","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T01:04:49-07:00","id":131771,"title":"","content":"If the player has the education, make him describe how it works. Tell him, out of character, that it has some appearance of impossibly fast natural healing, but the energy use can't be accounted for and wounds that would be impossible to heal naturally still seem to heal. Then let him fill in the gaps. Award experience to him for providing detail that enriches the game world.<br /> <br /> Essentially, he's immersing himself within his character - hypothesising scientific explanations to explain concepts that science can't explain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","user":"Bunyip","date":". 05-11-2014, 04:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T03:56:40-07:00","id":132024,"title":"","content":"That's good advice, Bunyip. Maybe he even discovers Essence as a byproduct of his investigation, that energy that is fueling the healing is greater than what the body is providing, where is it comming from?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}